<!DOCTYPE html><html  lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Stripe integration for AI agents and workflows | StackOS</title><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/_og/s/o_72fcgp.png"><meta name="twitter:image:src" content="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/_og/s/o_72fcgp.png"><meta property="og:image" content="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/_og/s/o_72fcgp.png"><meta property="og:image:type" content="image/png"><meta property="og:image:width" content="1200"><meta name="twitter:image:width" content="1200"><meta property="og:image:height" content="600"><meta name="twitter:image:height" content="600"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_nuxt/entry.HVu_FLFq.css" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_nuxt/_slug_.B6ti37_s.css" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_nuxt/useIntegrationCatalog.wtjwSlpy.css" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_nuxt/integrationRoutePolicy.BHfEqrhY.css" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_nuxt/LibraryFrame.CD2pOTex.css" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/fonts/manrope-latin-variable.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin="anonymous"><link rel="preload" as="fetch" crossorigin="anonymous" href="/library/integrations/stripe/_payload.json?aa586fb3-d485-480b-909f-6b016269cb06"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/CHhb2Wy-.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/Dpv_aybD.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/CxoQ3gne.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/B6iqfEGV.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/Df8p5hZf.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/C4_Tu-xR.js"><link rel="modulepreload" as="script" crossorigin href="/_nuxt/DHOT6Yra.js"><script type="module" src="/_nuxt/CHhb2Wy-.js" crossorigin></script><link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/images/stackos-icon.png"><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/images/stackos-icon.png"><link rel="alternate" type="application/rss+xml" title="StackOS Library" href="/feed.xml"><meta name="description" content="Stripe API transport for customers, invoices, payment lifecycle evidence, and balances. It contains no bookkeeping, collections, tax, or approval policy. Explore 37 listed Stripe actions and see how it fits into StackOS workflows."><meta name="theme-color" content="#090b10"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:title" content="Stripe integration for AI agents and workflows | StackOS"><meta property="og:description" content="Stripe API transport for customers, invoices, payment lifecycle evidence, and balances. It contains no bookkeeping, collections, tax, or approval policy. Explore 37 listed Stripe actions and see how it fits into StackOS workflows."><meta name="twitter:title" content="Stripe integration for AI agents and workflows | StackOS"><meta name="twitter:description" content="Stripe API transport for customers, invoices, payment lifecycle evidence, and balances. It contains no bookkeeping, collections, tax, or approval policy. Explore 37 listed Stripe actions and see how it fits into StackOS workflows."><meta name="robots" content="index, follow, max-image-preview:large, max-snippet:-1, max-video-preview:-1"><link rel="canonical" href="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/library/integrations/stripe/"><meta property="og:url" content="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/library/integrations/stripe/"><script type="application/ld+json" data-hid="integration-software">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"SoftwareApplication","name":"Stripe","description":"Stripe API transport for customers, invoices, payment lifecycle evidence, and balances. It contains no bookkeeping, collections, tax, or approval policy.","applicationCategory":"Finance Operations","url":"https://stripe.com/"}</script><script type="application/ld+json" data-hid="integration-faq">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What can the Stripe integration do in StackOS?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The current catalog includes 37 Stripe actions across Stripe invoicing, Stripe payment lifecycle evidence. The exact actions used depend on the workflow and approval rules."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does StackOS replace Stripe?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Stripe remains the tool that performs its part of the job. StackOS organizes the workflow, keeps status and dependencies visible, and calls the tool only when the plan reaches the right approved action."}}]}</script><meta property="og:site_name" content="StackOS"><script id="unhead:payload" type="application/json">{"titleTemplate":"%s | StackOS"}</script></head><body><div id="__nuxt"><!--[--><div id="top" class="site library-site" data-v-c771a7e2 data-v-e230b581><a class="skip-link" href="#main" data-v-e230b581>Skip to content</a><header class="site-header" data-v-e230b581><div class="shell site-header__inner"><a href="/" class="brand" aria-label="StackOS home"><img src="/images/stackos-icon.png" alt width="36" height="36"><span>StackOS</span><small>Work, organized</small></a><nav class="site-nav site-nav--desktop" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/#why" class="">Why StackOS</a><a href="/#workflow" class="">Workflows</a><a href="/#proof" class="">Product</a><a href="/getting-started/" class="">Get started</a><a href="/library/" class="">Library</a><a href="/#security" class="">Security</a><a class="button button--header" href="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/StackOS/stackos-latest-mac-arm64.dmg" data-download="stackos-mac"><img class="button__logo button__logo--apple" src="/images/apple.webp" alt="" width="18" height="18"> Download for Mac <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></nav><details class="mobile-menu"><summary role="button" aria-label="Toggle navigation" aria-controls="site-navigation"><span></span><span></span></summary><nav id="site-navigation" class="site-nav site-nav--mobile" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/#why" class="">Why StackOS</a><a href="/#workflow" class="">Workflows</a><a href="/#proof" class="">Product</a><a href="/getting-started/" class="">Get started</a><a href="/library/" class="">Library</a><a href="/#security" class="">Security</a><a class="button button--header" href="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/StackOS/stackos-latest-mac-arm64.dmg" data-download="stackos-mac"><img class="button__logo button__logo--apple" src="/images/apple.webp" alt="" width="18" height="18"> Download for Mac <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></nav></details></div></header><div class="library-nav" aria-label="Library sections" data-v-e230b581><div class="shell library-nav__inner" data-v-e230b581><a href="/library/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Library</a><a href="/library/workflows/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Workflows</a><a href="/library/agents/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Agents</a><a href="/library/orchestrators/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Orchestrators</a><a href="/library/integrations/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Integrations</a><a href="/library/articles/" class="" data-v-e230b581>Articles</a></div></div><main id="main" class="library-main" data-v-e230b581><nav class="library-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb" data-v-e230b581 data-v-59391fa3><div class="shell" data-v-59391fa3><ol data-v-59391fa3><!--[--><li data-v-59391fa3><a href="/" class="" data-v-59391fa3>Home</a></li><li data-v-59391fa3><a href="/library/" class="" data-v-59391fa3>Library</a></li><li data-v-59391fa3><a href="/library/integrations/" class="" data-v-59391fa3>Integrations</a></li><li data-v-59391fa3><a aria-current="page" href="/library/integrations/stripe/" class="router-link-active router-link-exact-active" data-v-59391fa3>Stripe</a></li><!--]--></ol></div></nav><!--[--><section class="integration-detail-hero" style="--integration-color:#635bff;" data-v-c771a7e2><div class="shell integration-detail-hero__grid" data-v-c771a7e2><div data-v-c771a7e2><div class="integration-detail-hero__identity" data-v-c771a7e2><span class="integration-mark is-large has-logo" style="--mark-color:#635bff;" aria-hidden="true" data-v-c771a7e2 data-v-aa7c01f7><img src="/images/integrations/stripe-icon.jpeg" alt="" data-v-aa7c01f7></span><div data-v-c771a7e2><a href="/library/integrations/plugins/finance/" class="" data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Finance Operations plugin</span></a><h1 data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe</h1></div></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe API transport for customers, invoices, payment lifecycle evidence, and balances. It contains no bookkeeping, collections, tax, or approval policy.</p><div class="integration-detail-hero__meta" data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2><strong data-v-c771a7e2>37</strong> listed actions</span><span data-v-c771a7e2><strong data-v-c771a7e2>2</strong> capability groups</span></div></div><aside data-v-c771a7e2><p data-v-c771a7e2>Use Stripe inside a complete plan.</p><strong data-v-c771a7e2>StackOS keeps the request, status, approvals, and proof connected around every tool action.</strong><div data-v-c771a7e2><!--[--><a href="https://stripe.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-v-c771a7e2>Visit tool <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-c771a7e2>↗</span></a><a href="https://docs.stripe.com/api" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-v-c771a7e2>Documentation <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-c771a7e2>↗</span></a><a href="https://dashboard.stripe.com/register" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-v-c771a7e2>Create account <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-c771a7e2>↗</span></a><a href="https://dashboard.stripe.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-v-c771a7e2>Open console <span aria-hidden="true" data-v-c771a7e2>↗</span></a><!--]--></div></aside></div></section><section class="integration-facts" data-provider-facts="stripe" data-v-c771a7e2><div class="shell" data-v-c771a7e2><div class="library-section__heading" data-v-c771a7e2><div data-v-c771a7e2><p class="eyebrow" data-v-c771a7e2>Connection facts</p><h2 data-v-c771a7e2>What the Stripe connector actually exposes.</h2></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>These details come from the current StackOS provider manifest and action catalog. They describe the available connection—not a promise that every workflow will use every action.</p></div><dl class="integration-facts__grid" data-v-c771a7e2><div data-v-c771a7e2><dt data-v-c771a7e2>Connection method</dt><dd data-v-c771a7e2>api-key</dd></div><div data-v-c771a7e2><dt data-v-c771a7e2>Setup</dt><dd data-v-c771a7e2>In the Stripe Dashboard, create a restricted API key with Product and Price reads for catalog selection and only the customer, invoice, invoice item, payment intent, payment record, charge, balance transaction, refund, and balance reads or writes required by your approved workflows. Connect it through StackOS; never share the key with an agent.</dd></div><div data-v-c771a7e2><dt data-v-c771a7e2>Capability groups</dt><dd data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing, Stripe payment lifecycle evidence</dd></div><div data-v-c771a7e2><dt data-v-c771a7e2>Action boundaries</dt><dd data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>25 read actions</span><span data-v-c771a7e2>12 write actions</span><!----><!----><!----></dd></div></dl></div></section><!----><!----><section class="integration-actions" data-v-c771a7e2><div class="shell" data-v-c771a7e2><div class="library-section__heading" data-v-c771a7e2><div data-v-c771a7e2><p class="eyebrow" data-v-c771a7e2>Action catalog</p><h2 data-v-c771a7e2>Actions listed for Stripe.</h2></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Actions listed for this integration. Individual descriptions note availability limits. A workflow still decides which actions belong in the job and where approval is required.</p></div><div class="integration-action-tools" data-v-c771a7e2><label for="action-query" data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Search Stripe actions</span><input id="action-query" value="" type="search" placeholder="Search 37 actions…" autocomplete="off" data-v-c771a7e2></label><div class="integration-action-tools__filters" data-v-c771a7e2><button class="is-active" type="button" data-v-c771a7e2>All <span data-v-c771a7e2>37</span></button><!--[--><button class="" type="button" data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing <span data-v-c771a7e2>21</span></button><button class="" type="button" data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe payment lifecycle evidence <span data-v-c771a7e2>16</span></button><!--]--></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>37 matching actions</p></div><div class="integration-action-grid" data-v-c771a7e2><!--[--><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Attach Stripe Payment to Invoice</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe payment lifecycle evidence</span><b class="is-write" data-v-c771a7e2>Can make changes</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Attach exactly one previously verified PaymentIntent or PaymentRecord to one invoice. Allocation and matching decisions remain in the workflow.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Clean Up Stripe Invoice PDF Transfer</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing</span><b class="is-write" data-v-c771a7e2>Can make changes</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Delete one private invoice PDF staging transfer by opaque reference, within the current project and Stripe account. Call only after external evidence custody and SHA-256 verification; never deletes external finance evidence or contacts Stripe.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Create Draft Stripe Invoice</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing</span><b class="is-write" data-v-c771a7e2>Can make changes</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Create a Stripe draft invoice in the explicitly approved currency that will later be explicitly finalized and sent.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Create Stripe Customer</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing</span><b class="is-write" data-v-c771a7e2>Can make changes</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Create one Stripe customer from explicit approved details and return an account-bound customer reference.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Create Stripe Customer Tax ID</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing</span><b class="is-write" data-v-c771a7e2>Can make changes</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Create exactly one explicitly approved tax ID after an independently completed duplicate check. The connector performs no lookup, normalization, tax decision or retry. Reuse the exact idempotency key on an authorized retry and independently retrieve the result; creation does not establish verification or update issued invoice snapshots.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Create Stripe Invoice Item</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing</span><b class="is-write" data-v-c771a7e2>Can make changes</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Add one explicit draft line using either a positive manual amount or an existing account-bound Stripe price and explicit quantity.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Download Finalized Stripe Invoice PDF</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Retrieve the exact account-bound invoice and download its finalized PDF into private temporary local staging. Refuses drafts; never finalizes or sends. Copy the returned local file to external finance evidence storage, verify its SHA-256, then clean up the transfer. The staged file is not a public media artifact or delivery evidence.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Finalize Stripe Invoice</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing</span><b class="is-write" data-v-c771a7e2>Can make changes</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Finalize one reviewed draft invoice with auto_advance=false; this does not send it.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>List Stripe Balance Transactions</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe payment lifecycle evidence</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Return one bounded Stripe balance transaction page with gross, fee, refund, and net evidence.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>List Stripe Charges</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe payment lifecycle evidence</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Return one bounded Stripe charge page and a safe continuation reference, optionally filtered by customer or payment intent.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>List Stripe Customer Tax IDs</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Read one bounded page of one customer&#39;s tax IDs, with safe refs, exact value hashes and observed verification status. Exhaust all pages and compare type plus exact value hash before deciding whether an approved identifier is absent; there is no atomic uniqueness guarantee.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>List Stripe Customers by Exact Email</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Return one bounded page of Stripe customers matching one exact email, so an existing customer can be used without a raw provider ID.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>List Stripe Disputes</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe payment lifecycle evidence</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Read one bounded dispute page for exactly one charge or payment intent; no evidence content or dispute mutation is exposed.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>List Stripe Invoice Items</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Read one bounded page of items for exactly one invoice or customer; descriptions are exact UTF-8 SHA-256 digests by default, with optional scoped business text.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>List Stripe Invoice Payments</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe payment lifecycle evidence</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Return bounded payment lifecycle evidence for one Stripe invoice. Missing or null payment linkage preserves facts and pagination but cannot establish a payment match or settlement.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>List Stripe Invoices</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Return one bounded Stripe invoice page and a safe continuation reference when more results exist.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>List Stripe Payment Records</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe payment lifecycle evidence</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Temporarily unavailable in StackOS while the documented Stripe PaymentRecord listing endpoint availability mismatch is resolved. Inspect retained action audit/response files and retrieve a known PaymentRecord ref; if the ref is missing, hold for owner/provider recovery and never create a replacement report.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>List Stripe Prices</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Read one bounded catalog page preserving price type, currency and pricing structure; optionally include nickname and lookup key.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>List Stripe Products</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Read one bounded catalog page with safe product and default-price references; optionally include product name, description, and unit label.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>List Stripe Refunds</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe payment lifecycle evidence</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Return one bounded Stripe refund page for reconciliation evidence; this action never creates refunds.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Mark Stripe Invoice Paid Out of Band</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe payment lifecycle evidence</span><b class="is-write" data-v-c771a7e2>Can make changes</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Mark one verified fully settled invoice paid without creating a Stripe charge. It is never a partial-settlement fallback.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Report Verified Stripe Payment Record</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe payment lifecycle evidence</span><b class="is-write" data-v-c771a7e2>Can make changes</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Report one verified bank transfer with a fixed custom Bank transfer method and guaranteed outcome. The bank reference is materialized only for provider dispatch and is never returned.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Retrieve Stripe Balance</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe payment lifecycle evidence</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Retrieve current available and pending Stripe balance buckets for cashflow evidence; it never moves funds.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Retrieve Stripe Balance Transaction</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe payment lifecycle evidence</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Retrieve gross, fee, and net evidence for one previously discovered Stripe balance transaction.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Retrieve Stripe Charge</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe payment lifecycle evidence</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Retrieve one previously discovered Stripe charge by its safe reference; optionally include its description, receipt link and safe customer reference for matching.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Retrieve Stripe Customer</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Retrieve one previously discovered Stripe customer by an account-bound reference; return exact billing-detail and ordered invoice custom-field digests for independent readback, with optional sensitive business details. Customer defaults do not rewrite finalized invoice snapshots.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Retrieve Stripe Customer Tax ID</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Independently read one account- and customer-bound tax ID. Report actual provider verification status, including pending, unavailable, unverified or null; do not infer verified from successful creation.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Retrieve Stripe Dispute</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe payment lifecycle evidence</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Read a previously discovered dispute by its account-bound reference, excluding submitted evidence and customer content.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Retrieve Stripe Invoice</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Retrieve one invoice with its current customer expanded, customer snapshot digests, observed due date, footer digest, PaymentIntent method list, and hosted/PDF link availability states. recipient_pay_online_button_state=unverified never proves the button absent; draft_dashboard_link_state=not_exposed_by_stripe_api means no stable saved-draft review link is returned. For a draft PDF, inspect the selected invoice manually in Stripe Dashboard and verify whether its Download PDF action is available. Optional business details include invoice number, memo, customer snapshot name/email and available hosted invoice/PDF URLs; additional billing recipients remain outside API visibility.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Retrieve Stripe Payment Intent</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe payment lifecycle evidence</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Retrieve verified PaymentIntent settlement evidence by an account-bound reference, excluding payment method, PII, metadata, and client-secret data.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Retrieve Stripe Payment Record</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe payment lifecycle evidence</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Retrieve one reported PaymentRecord by an account-bound reference, exposing only settlement state, safe account references, and a bank-reference digest.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Retrieve Stripe Price</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Read an account-bound price with fixed tier and currency-option expansions; preserve pricing facts without computing totals.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Retrieve Stripe Product</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Read one account-bound product and its default-price reference, with optional selected business details.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Retrieve Stripe Refund</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe payment lifecycle evidence</span><b class="is-read" data-v-c771a7e2>Reads data</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Retrieve one previously discovered Stripe refund; this action never creates a refund.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Send Stripe Invoice</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing</span><b class="is-write" data-v-c771a7e2>Can make changes</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Request Stripe customer delivery for one finalized invoice; the API has no operator-review recipient override and does not document inheriting Dashboard Email invoice without link. Never use this action to send a review copy or assume a Dashboard-only choice makes this API route no-link. Sandbox/test mode sends no email; an accepted test request is not sent/delivered. Live acceptance is not inbox-delivery proof. Workflow approval and exception policy remain outside the connector.</p></article><article data-v-c771a7e2><h3 data-v-c771a7e2>Update Stripe Customer Billing Details</h3><div data-v-c771a7e2><span data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe invoicing</span><b class="is-write" data-v-c771a7e2>Can make changes</b></div><p data-v-c771a7e2>Update only selected fields of one existing customer. Custom fields replace the entire list; independently retrieve current defaults, preserve every unrelated field in the approved replacement, then retrieve again to verify exact values. Customer defaults do not rewrite existing finalized invoices; independently inspect each invoice snapshot.</p></article><!--]--></div><button class="integration-load-more" type="button" data-v-c771a7e2> Show 36 more <span data-v-c771a7e2>(1 remaining)</span></button></div></section><section class="integration-answer" data-v-c771a7e2><div class="detail-body__narrow" data-v-c771a7e2><p class="eyebrow" data-v-c771a7e2>Direct answer</p><h2 data-v-c771a7e2>How does the Stripe integration work?</h2><p data-v-c771a7e2>People continue using Stripe as their tool. StackOS adds it to a visible workflow, keeps the work in order, and passes only the approved action to the integration when that stage is ready.</p><ol class="integration-route-flow" style="--route-color:#635bff;" data-integration-route="stripe" aria-label="How StackOS routes approved work to Stripe" data-v-c771a7e2 data-v-4eb1f27f><!--[--><li data-v-4eb1f27f><span data-v-4eb1f27f>01</span><strong data-v-4eb1f27f>Your request</strong><small data-v-4eb1f27f>Start in your AI</small></li><li data-v-4eb1f27f><span data-v-4eb1f27f>02</span><strong data-v-4eb1f27f>StackOS plan</strong><small data-v-4eb1f27f>Expands the steps</small></li><li data-v-4eb1f27f><span data-v-4eb1f27f>03</span><strong data-v-4eb1f27f>Stripe</strong><small data-v-4eb1f27f>Does its bounded part</small></li><li data-v-4eb1f27f><span data-v-4eb1f27f>04</span><strong data-v-4eb1f27f>Checked result</strong><small data-v-4eb1f27f>Keeps the proof</small></li><!--]--></ol></div></section><!----><section class="integration-faq" aria-labelledby="integration-faq-title" data-v-c771a7e2><div class="detail-body__narrow" data-v-c771a7e2><p class="eyebrow" data-v-c771a7e2>Common questions</p><h2 id="integration-faq-title" data-v-c771a7e2>Stripe and StackOS.</h2><!--[--><details data-v-c771a7e2><summary data-v-c771a7e2>What can the Stripe integration do in StackOS?</summary><p data-v-c771a7e2>The current catalog includes 37 Stripe actions across Stripe invoicing, Stripe payment lifecycle evidence. The exact actions used depend on the workflow and approval rules.</p></details><details data-v-c771a7e2><summary data-v-c771a7e2>Does StackOS replace Stripe?</summary><p data-v-c771a7e2>No. Stripe remains the tool that performs its part of the job. StackOS organizes the workflow, keeps status and dependencies visible, and calls the tool only when the plan reaches the right approved action.</p></details><!--]--></div></section><!--]--></main><footer class="site-footer" data-v-e230b581 data-v-5f58f905><div class="shell site-footer__grid" data-v-5f58f905><a href="/" class="footer-brand" data-v-5f58f905><img src="/images/stackos-icon.png" alt width="42" height="42" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-v-5f58f905><div data-v-5f58f905><strong data-v-5f58f905>StackOS</strong><span data-v-5f58f905>Keep AI-powered work clear, connected, and moving.</span></div></a><div class="site-footer__links" data-v-5f58f905><div data-v-5f58f905><span data-v-5f58f905>Explore</span><a href="/#why" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Why StackOS</a><a href="/getting-started/" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Getting started</a><a href="/library/" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Library</a><a href="/library/workflows/" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Workflows</a><a href="/library/articles/" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Articles</a></div><div data-v-5f58f905><span data-v-5f58f905>Build</span><a href="/#security" class="" data-v-5f58f905>Security</a><a href="https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/StackOS/stackos-latest-mac-arm64.dmg" data-download="stackos-mac" data-v-5f58f905>Download</a><a href="https://github.com/flowmonkeyio/StackOS" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" data-v-5f58f905>GitHub ↗</a></div></div><div class="site-footer__status" data-v-5f58f905><span class="status-dot" data-v-5f58f905></span><div data-v-5f58f905><strong data-v-5f58f905>Runs on your Mac</strong><small data-v-5f58f905>Your work. Your apps. Your private logins.</small></div></div></div><div class="shell site-footer__bottom" data-v-5f58f905><span data-v-5f58f905>StackOS · Your AI tool works. StackOS keeps the work organized.</span><span data-v-5f58f905>Runs locally.</span></div></footer></div><!----><!--]--></div><div id="teleports"></div><script>window.__NUXT__={};window.__NUXT__.config={public:{siteUrl:"https://stackos.flowmonkey.io",gaMeasurementId:"G-KPZXCGXGG5",downloadUrl:"https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/StackOS/stackos-latest-mac-arm64.dmg",scripts:{googleAnalytics:{id:"G-KPZXCGXGG5",scriptOptions:{bundle:false}}},"nuxt-scripts":{version:"",prefix:"/_scripts",defaultScriptOptions:{trigger:"onNuxtReady"},googleStaticMapsProxy:"",endpoints:{}},mdc:{components:{prose:true,map:{},customElements:[]},headings:{anchorLinks:{h1:false,h2:true,h3:true,h4:true,h5:false,h6:false}},highlight:false},"nuxt-seo-utils-version":"8.3.1","seo-utils":{canonicalQueryWhitelist:["page","sort","filter","search","q","category","tag"],canonicalLowercase:true,tagPriority:"low",separator:"",titleSeparator:""},content:{wsUrl:""},"nuxt-robots":{version:"6.1.2",isNuxtContentV2:false,debug:false,credits:true,groups:[{userAgent:["*"],disallow:[""],allow:[],contentUsage:[],contentSignal:[],_indexable:true,_rules:[],_normalized:true}],sitemap:["/sitemap.xml"],header:true,robotsEnabledValue:"index, follow, max-image-preview:large, max-snippet:-1, max-video-preview:-1",robotsDisabledValue:"noindex, nofollow",cacheControl:"max-age=14400, must-revalidate",botDetection:true,pageMetaRobots:{}},"nuxt-og-image":{defaults:{emojis:"noto",extension:"png",width:1200,height:600,cacheMaxAgeSeconds:259200},hasServerRuntime:false}},app:{baseURL:"/",buildId:"aa586fb3-d485-480b-909f-6b016269cb06",buildAssetsDir:"/_nuxt/",cdnURL:""}}</script><script type="application/ld+json" data-nuxt-schema-org="true" data-hid="schema-org-graph">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@id":"https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/#website","@type":"WebSite","description":"The place where AI-powered work becomes clear, connected, and accountable.","inLanguage":"en","name":"StackOS","url":"https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/","publisher":{"@id":"https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/#identity"}},{"@id":"https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/library/integrations/stripe/#webpage","@type":"WebPage","description":"Stripe API transport for customers, invoices, payment lifecycle evidence, and balances. It contains no bookkeeping, collections, tax, or approval policy.","name":"Stripe integration","url":"https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/library/integrations/stripe/","about":{"@id":"https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/#identity"},"breadcrumb":{"@id":"https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/library/integrations/stripe/#breadcrumb"},"isPartOf":{"@id":"https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/#website"},"potentialAction":[{"@type":"ReadAction","target":["https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/library/integrations/stripe/"]}]},{"@id":"https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/#identity","@type":"Organization","description":"The local operating layer for clear, connected, and accountable AI-powered work.","name":"StackOS","url":"https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/","image":{"@id":"https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/#/schema/image/1"},"sameAs":["https://github.com/flowmonkeyio/StackOS"]},{"@id":"https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/library/integrations/stripe/#breadcrumb","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","name":"Home","item":"https://stackos.flowmonkey.io","position":1},{"@type":"ListItem","name":"Library","item":"https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/library/","position":2},{"@type":"ListItem","name":"Integrations","item":"https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/library/integrations/","position":3},{"@type":"ListItem","name":"Stripe","item":"https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/library/integrations/stripe/","position":4}]},{"@id":"https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/#/schema/image/1","@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/images/stackos-icon.png","inLanguage":"en","url":"https://stackos.flowmonkey.io/images/stackos-icon.png"}]}</script><script type="application/json" data-nuxt-data="nuxt-app" data-ssr="true" id="__NUXT_DATA__" data-src="/library/integrations/stripe/_pa